{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Do not turn to their offering.</b> Do not turn to any kind of offering they may bring to gain atonement — the opposite of יֵרַח מִנְחָה (1 Samuel 26:19) (turn toward an offering). This is because I do not forgive the insult to me, and their sin cannot be forgiven without this, as the Sages said: עֲוֹנוֹת שֶׁבֵּין אָדָם לַחֲבֵרוֹ אֵין יוֹם הַכִּפּוּרִים מְכַפֵּר עַד שֶׁיְּרַצֶּה חֲבֵרוֹ (Yoma 85a). And so Jeremiah said: אַל תְּכַפֵּר עַל עֲוֹנָם וְחַטָּאתָם מִלְּפָנֶיךָ אַל תֶּמְחִי, כִּי כָרוּ שִׁיחָה לְלָכְדֵנִי. זְכוֹר עָמְדִי לְפָנֶיךָ לְדַבֵּר עֲלֵיהֶם טוֹבָה (Jeremiah 18:20–23)." "<b>Nor have I taken a single donkey from them.</b> I did not benefit from them even in what one ordinary person benefits from another, for I did not accept from them even a donkey on loan. If so, my authority over them was entirely for their benefit and to set their affairs right — not for my benefit or enjoyment at all, as is the way of all who hold authority. They are not resentful of my authority except from the side of their being ungrateful." "<b>Nor have I harmed a single one of them.</b> They have no claim against me even for hatred of one who emerges from court guilty — for it never happened that they came before me for judgment in a manner that I would find them liable."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:40:11.792330061Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}